<title>UK: LONDON TEA AUCTION PRICE INDICATIONS.</title>
<headline>LONDON TEA AUCTION PRICE INDICATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>At today's London landed Tea Auction of 3,650 packages of 53.50 kgs, including 1,600 offshore, price indications in pence a kilo compared to the last sale and the corresponding week last year.</p>
<p>    Best available  178   (230 and 174)</p>
<p>    Good		170   (175 and 116)</p>
<p>    Good Medium     165   (165 and 112)</p>
<p>    Medium	    155   (152 and 104)</p>
<p>    Low Medium	125   (120 and  86)</p>
<p>The highest price paid was 178 pence for a Burundi PD.</p>
</text>
